From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:50:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: end the context on a required handle that arrives as
 object id 0

The codec yields NULL for a non-dispatchable handle that the guest sends as
object id 0, and refuses only an id that names no object of the type, plus
id 0 for the first argument of a command.  A handle the specification does
not allow to be VK_NULL_HANDLE therefore reaches its handler as a null
pointer, which the renderer reads or the driver dereferences, and in the
product the renderer runs in the app's own process.

Add vkr_context_refuse_null_handle(), which logs the command and the slot
and ends the context as an id that names no object does, and ask it in the
handlers this project wrote or changed and in the few upstream ones that
read the handle themselves: the memory requirements and binds of buffers
and images (a bind with no memory is refused outright, since the swapchain
binding that allows one is not in the protocol), vkCreateImageView's
conversion, vkCmdCopyMemoryToImageKHR, vkCmdCopyImageToMemoryKHR and
vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResultsToMemoryKHR, vkFreeCommandBuffers and
vkFreeDescriptorSets, vkImportSemaphoreResourceMESA, vkCreateFramebuffer's
render pass, the physical devices of a device group, and the libraries a
pipeline create info chains, and a create info that chains pipeline
binaries.  The renderer serves no VK_KHR_pipeline_binary, so no object
names a binary, and a guest can enable the extension on a device by name.
The bind commands also refuse an array the codec left null.

vkCmdCopyMemoryToImageKHR and vkCmdCopyImageToMemoryKHR may send no info at
all, which the driver ignores, so the image of the info is read only when the
info is there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
